\description{
Check SDRF-Proteomics files against the specification's structural rules, one row per finding.

One bridge process for the whole corpus instead of one per file, with the parallelism inside
the bridge where it belongs. The result does not depend on \code{threads}: rows are always in input
order.
}
\value{
An \code{mzlibr_sdrf_validation_batch}: \code{file_count} documents given, \code{read_count}
  documents validated, \code{failed_count} documents that could not be read, \code{valid_count} documents
  read with no \code{Error}, \code{message_count} findings over every document read, \code{record_count} rows
  in \code{records}, and \code{caveats}.

  \code{records} has the columns of \code{\link{sdrf_validate}}'s, preceded by \code{source_index} - the document's
  1-based position in \code{paths}, so it indexes \code{files} - and \code{source_path}. \code{files} has one row per
  input: \code{path}, \code{is_valid}, \code{error_count}, \code{warning_count}, \code{message_count}, \code{row_count}, and
  \code{error_kind} / \code{error_message}, which are \code{NA} for a document that was read. A document that
  was not read has \code{NA} for every count.

