\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item STRUCTURE ONLY: column presence, order, casing, cell shape and row-key uniqueness against v1.1.0. Controlled-vocabulary accessions are not resolved.
\item Severities were calibrated by mzLib against the 1,236-file bigbio curated corpus; a rule that fired on most curated files was demoted, not the files condemned.
\item A document of reserved words validates cleanly. Use sdrf assess for whether it says anything, sdrf lint for whether several agree.
}
}
\section{Performance}{
Every call starts one bridge process, which costs a .NET start-up before any work. This bulk form pays it once for the whole list, which is the reason it exists: never loop the one-path function over many files.
}
